{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The driver's own 30-day record trips the POL-NS-07 anti-farming check on BOTH of its conjunctive limbs: driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d is 5, which is '4 or more', and 5 divided by driver_profile.completed_trips_30d of 40 is 0.125, which is greater than 0.08. Compensation must therefore be WITHHELD, the case escalates under POL-NS-09, and the escalation packet must direct the reviewer to refund this rider's cancellation fee in full. The very pattern the check exists to intercept - five no-show terminations inside a month of 40 completed trips - is the pattern that produced the $4.00 charged to this rider, and it is the rider who should not be left funding it.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-DPROF-00409", "EV-FARE-00409"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-07", "POL-NS-09"],
      "relies_on": "driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The POL-NS-07 check reads the trailing-window counters driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d and driver_profile.completed_trips_30d, and the clause says in terms that no other profile field may be used for it: driver_profile.prior_no_show_flags is a lifetime counter and is not the trailing-30-day figure. Substituting the lifetime counter for the trailing one is forbidden by POL-GEN-01, so the driver cannot escape the check by pointing at a lifetime value of 1. On the counters the clause actually names - 5 terminations against 40 completed trips - the withholding branch is engaged.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-DPROF-00409"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-07", "POL-GEN-01"],
      "relies_on": "driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Escalation under POL-NS-09 is terminal and, per POL-GEN-03, replaces any monetary ruling: no refund and no compensation issue, and the disputed $4.00 is held rather than finally collected or refunded while the review is pending, with the rider's full refund written into the packet as an instruction to the reviewer. That is the outcome this record supports. The ledger in EV-FARE-00409 shows payment_status CHARGED, a cancellation_fee of 4.00 and refund_issued_sgd of 0.00, so NO_ACTION - which by POL-GEN-03 leaves the present state exactly as it is - would leave this rider carrying the charge off a driver whose 30-day no-show record is under examination.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00409"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-03", "POL-NS-09"],
      "relies_on": "fare_breakdown.payment_status",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "EV-ADVIS-00409-01 is MISSING - no traffic advisory covers Kallang Bahru in this window - and it carries weight 0.0 with the issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT, so I disclose that impairment on the face of this claim. Under POL-NS-06(i) waiting time may be accumulated across separate in-geofence intervals only where a traffic_advisory is present and populated and carries a qualifying type; a MISSING advisory makes that limb unavailable, so none of the driver's time here can be extended, topped up or excused by a kerb restriction, an enforcement operation or a closure. The clause also says that asserting the limb against the MISSING artifact triggers POL-NS-09 rather than exonerating anyone - which is a second, independent route to the same escalation.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-00409-01", "EV-GPS-00409"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-06"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.accumulated_dwell.limb.available",
      "asserted_weight": 0.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The arrival marker on this trip is BUTTON, not GPS_AUTO, so POL-NS-12's platform-confirmed arrival route is not open to the driver: both arrival and the waiting clock have to be made out from the exported trace under POL-NS-02 and POL-NS-05. That trace shows a single continuous in-geofence run of 330 seconds against the 300-second minimum in force for this STANDARD pickup, and the driver cancelled 30 seconds after it elapsed. The charge therefore rests entirely on a 30-second margin recorded by the driver's own device - exactly the thin, self-recorded no-show that the 30-day check under POL-NS-07 must be run on before this rider's money moves.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-00409", "EV-GPS-00409"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-12", "POL-NS-05", "POL-NS-07"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.longest_qualifying_run.duration_sec",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "ESCALATE",
    "amount_sgd": null,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [
      "POL-NS-07 (anti-farming branch, escalation packet): direct the human reviewer to refund the rider's cancellation fee of SGD 4.00 in full; the SGD 4.00 stays held — neither collected nor refunded by the automated pipeline — while that review is pending."
    ],
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "To the rider: on the driving record this was a validly chargeable no-show, so your claim that you came down promptly is not made out. EV-TRIP-00409 shows the driver's arrival marker at 23:36:20 on 23 August 2026, and EV-GPS-00409 places him inside the 50 m STANDARD pickup radius from that instant (34 qualifying fixes, single uninterrupted in-geofence run, so the police under POL-NS-05 finds no false marker). The free waiting period in force for this trip is 300 seconds, read from the record's own platform_policy.free_wait_sec, and the measured dwell is 330 seconds; the driver cancelled at 23:41:50 under the code RIDER_NO_SHOW, exactly as that dwell elapsed. POL-NS-01 limbs (a) to (d) therefore all hold, and the SGD 4.00 fee was chargeable. Your side's contrary claims fail: EV-GPS-00409's rider track shows your device stationary about 636 m from the pickup pin for the whole window with no qualifying fix inside the 100 m rider-presence radius, and EV-CHAT-00409 shows no locating or coordinating message from you, while the driver both messaged 'arrived blk 27' at 23:36:35 and placed a 20-second in-app call at 23:39:20 that went unanswered — so POL-NS-04 exonerates nobody. POL-NS-03 is not engaged (the driver's stationary fixes are inside the radius, not outside it), POL-NS-06 gives you nothing because the 330-second dwell exceeds the 300-second minimum by 30 seconds, and POL-NS-12 is correctly said to be closed because this was a driver-pressed BUTTON marker, not a GPS_AUTO arrival. The MISSING traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-00409-01 (weight 0.0, issue MISSING_ARTIFACT) makes POL-NS-06(i) unavailable and, as both sides say, cannot exonerate anyone or extend the clock; it is not what decides this case.\n\nTo the driver: POL-NS-01 is satisfied in full on your own record, but your payout does not issue. POL-NS-07's anti-farming check reads driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d = 5 and completed_trips_30d = 40: 5 is '4 or more' and 5/40 = 0.125 exceeds 0.08, so both limbs trip, the 80 percent payout of SGD 3.20 on the SGD 4.00 fee is WITHHELD, and the case escalates under POL-NS-09(d). This is not a finding that you did not attend. Your lifetime prior_no_show_flags of 1 is not the field that check reads, and your rating, acceptance rate and cancellation rate are context only; the two trailing-window counters are the only fields the clause permits, exactly as both advocate sides agreed. \n\nTo both parties: escalation under POL-NS-09 is terminal and replaces any monetary outcome, so no refund and no compensation issue now and the SGD 4.00 is held rather than collected or refunded. The packet carries the instruction POL-NS-07 requires — that the reviewer refund the rider's SGD 4.00 cancellation fee in full. Both parties have the POL-GEN-04 appeal route, and because escalation is terminal the case goes to human review under POL-GEN-06. Confidence is 0.90; the deciding artifacts (EV-TRIP-00409, EV-GPS-00409, EV-CHAT-00409, EV-FARE-00409, EV-DPROF-00409) are all COMPLETE at weight_multiplier 1.0, so nothing in this ruling rests on impaired evidence and the 0.70 floor is not in play."
  },
  "discarded_claims": [
    {
      "claim": "POL-NS-06 gives the rider no route to a refund: the derived shortfall is negative 30 seconds, that is, the measured dwell exceeds the required minimum by 30 seconds, so there is no waiting-period shortfall to refund. I note for completeness that limb (i)'s accumulation route is unavailable because EV-ADVIS-00409-01 is MISSING and carries weight 0.0 — a missing advisory cannot be asserted — but it is not needed here, because the 330 seconds was one continuous in-geofence run.",
      "side": "DRIVER",
      "reason_code": "IMPAIRMENT_UNDISCLOSED",
      "detail": "the claim cites impaired artifact EV-ADVIS-00409-01 at weight_multiplier 0.0 but does not name its issue code(s): MISSING_ARTIFACT"
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "ESCALATE",
    "amount_sgd": null,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [
      "POL-NS-07 (anti-farming withholding, escalation under POL-NS-09(d)): the escalation packet directs the human reviewer to refund the rider's cancellation fee of SGD 4.00 in full; pending that review the SGD 4.00 is held and is neither collected from the rider nor paid out to the driver."
    ],
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "To both parties. This ruling moves no money today; the SGD 4.00 in dispute is held, and the reason is set out below.\n\nWhat the record establishes. The driver reached Blk 27 Kallang Bahru at 23:36:20 on 23 August and held position inside the 50 m STANDARD pickup radius until he cancelled at 23:41:50 — a single continuous in-geofence dwell of 330 seconds (GPS trace EV-GPS-00409, trip record EV-TRIP-00409). The free waiting period in force for this trip is 300 seconds, read from the record's own platform_policy.free_wait_sec and not from the 180-second default, so the driver held position 30 seconds past the minimum. The arrival marker was pressed at the first qualifying in-geofence fix (dwell start offset 0.0 s), the trace never shows the driver travelling at 15 km/h or more, and the trip was terminated at 23:41:50 under reason code RIDER_NO_SHOW, one of the three codes POL-NS-01 recognises; the record's no_show_threshold_sec is null. All four limbs of POL-NS-01 hold, and on the merits alone the SGD 4.00 fee was chargeable.\n\nThe rider's account is not supported. The rider says he came down within a few minutes. His own device says otherwise: 37 rider fixes, none of them inside the 100 m rider-presence radius for a STANDARD pickup, stationary about 640 m from the pickup pin across the whole waiting window. POL-NS-04 therefore cannot exonerate him — he sent no locating or coordinating message, and the driver both wrote 'arrived blk 27' at 23:36:35 and placed an in-app call at 23:39:20 that went unanswered. POL-NS-03 does not apply, because the driver's stationary fixes were inside the arrival radius, not outside it. POL-NS-06 gives no refund: 330 seconds exceeds the 300-second minimum, so there is no shortfall, and because the 330 seconds was one continuous run, limb (i)'s accumulation route is not needed — the missing advisory EV-ADVIS-00409-01 (weight 0.0, issue MISSING_ARTIFACT) is correctly disclosed but carries no fact and decides nothing here.\n\nWhy the case still escalates. POL-NS-07's anti-farming check reads only driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d, which is 5 (4 or more), and driver_profile.completed_trips_30d, which is 40, giving 5 / 40 = 0.125, above the 0.08 rate. Both limbs trip on both advocates' arithmetic, so the driver's compensation of SGD 3.20 (80 percent of the SGD 4.00 fee in force) is WITHHELD and the case escalates under POL-NS-09(d). The lifetime counter prior_no_show_flags (1) may not be substituted for the trailing-30-day figure, and neither party's rating, acceptance rate or cancellation rate bears on this test — POL-GEN-01 makes all of those context only.\n\nWhat this means for each of you. No payment issues: the SGD 4.00 is held rather than collected from the rider or released to the driver. The escalation packet directs the human reviewer to refund the rider's SGD 4.00 in full, so that the rider does not fund a dispute the platform has not resolved. The open question the reviewer must settle is whether five no-show terminations in 30 days against 40 completed trips reflects fee-farming rather than genuine no-shows. No artifact relied on is impaired under POL-NS-08 — the arrived event matches the first qualifying GPS fix to the second, the trace carries 68 fixes at 10-second cadence with no gap, the chat log holds 3 messages matching the record's chat_message_count of 3, and the ledger's SGD 4.00 cancellation line reconciles with the SGD 4.00 fee in force — so POL-NS-09(e) is not engaged and the escalation rests on the driver-profile check alone. Confidence 0.9: the deciding facts are carried by artifacts at weight 1.0 (EV-TRIP-00409, EV-GPS-00409, EV-DPROF-00409), so the POL-GEN-02(2) cap is 1.0."
  },
  "discarded_claims": [
    {
      "claim": "POL-NS-06 gives the rider no route to a refund: the derived shortfall is negative 30 seconds, that is, the measured dwell exceeds the required minimum by 30 seconds, so there is no waiting-period shortfall to refund. I note for completeness that limb (i)'s accumulation route is unavailable because EV-ADVIS-00409-01 is MISSING and carries weight 0.0 — a missing advisory cannot be asserted — but it is not needed here, because the 330 seconds was one continuous in-geofence run.",
      "side": "DRIVER",
      "reason_code": "IMPAIRMENT_UNDISCLOSED",
      "detail": "the claim cites impaired artifact EV-ADVIS-00409-01 at weight_multiplier 0.0 but does not name its issue code(s): MISSING_ARTIFACT"
    }
  ]
}
